TI  - Relationship between Quantitative Measurement of <i>Porphyromonas gingivalis</i> on Dental Plaque with Periodontal Status of Patients with Coronary Heart Disease
T2  - BIOMEDICAL ENGINEERING'S RECENT PROGRESS IN BIOMATERIALS, DRUGS DEVELOPMENT, AND MEDICAL DEVICES
CP  - 1st International Symposium of Biomedical Engineering (ISBE)
AB  - Coronary heart disease is a narrowing of coronary artery due to plaque build-up. [1] Chronic periodontitis increases risk of cardiovascular disease. P. gingivalis is linked to both diseases. Objective: to analyse quantitative difference of P. gingivalis on dental plaque and its relationship with periodontal status of CHD patient and control. Methods: Periodontal status of 66 CHD patient and 40 control was checked. Subgingival plaque was isolated and P. gingivalis was measured using real-time PCR. Result: P. gingivalis of CHD patient differs from control. P. gingivalis is linked to pocket depth of CHD patient. Conclusion: P. gingivalis count of CHD patient is higher than control. P. gingivalis count is not linked to any periodontal status, except for pocket depth of CHD patient.
