TI  - Lipid regulation in elderly hyperlipidemic patients - Results with etofyllin clofibrate
T2  - PERFUSION
AB  - The objective of the present study was to evaluate the efficacy and the tolerance of the lipid lowering compound etofyllin clofibrate (Duolip(R) 500) in elderly hyperlipidemic patients. Data from 1862 male and female patients in the age of 61 to 95 years with lipid disorders, who had entered a drug monitoring were analyzed. After treatment for 3 to 4 month with 500 mg etofyllin clofibrate, s.i.d., HDL-cholesterol which is of particular importance in older patients increased by 26.4%. At the same time plasma cholesterol, LDL-cholesterol and serum triglycerides fell by 16.4%, 19.3% and 29.1%, respectively. The ratio of total plasma- to HDL-cholesterol decreased by 30.2%. Only 2.8% of all patients reported side effects, mainly mild gastrointestinal complaints. This evaluation shows that etofyllin clofibrate improves prognostically unfavourable lipid parameters in older patients in an effective and safe way and hence improves important risk factors for mortality and morbidity associated with coronary heart disease.
