TI  - ENTEROSORPTION IN CORRECTION OF DYSLIPOPROTEINEMIAS IN CORONARY PATIENTS OF ADVANCED AGE
T2  - KLINICHESKAYA MEDITSINA
AB  - Sixty patients with coronary heart disease, stable angina pectoris of functional class II and III and dislipoproteinemia (cholesterol > 6.5 mmol/l, triglycerides > 2.0 mmol/l, the atherogenic index > 3.5) were assigned to two groups.  40 patients received enterosorbent (high-porous, small-spherical fraction of CKH carbon).  20 control subjects were treated with placebo.  The patients' age ranged from 60 to 74.  The treatment course lasted for 4 weeks.  Evaluation of the treatment results showed that total cholesterol dropped by 20 %, triglycerides by 27 %, apoB by 32 %, apoB-conteining lipoproteins by 20 %; there were positive changes in circulation, clinical status (in 60 % of cases), exercise tolerance (by 12 %).  Control patients did not present any noticeable shifts.  Thus, enterosorption proved an effective modality of dyslipoproteinemia correction in coronary patients of advanced age.
