TY  - JOUR
AU  - Rose, P
AU  - Elsasser, R
TI  - Etofyllin clofibrate improves the metabolism of lipids and glucose in patients with hyerlipidemia and diabetes
T2  - MEDIZINISCHE WELT
AB  - The objective of the present clinical investigation was to evaluate the effects of the lipid lowering drug etofyllin clofibrate (Duolip(R) 500) on metabolism of-lipids and glucose in patients with hyperlipidemia and diabetes. Fdr that purpose, data from 1200 male and female patients, who had been participated in a drug-monitoring, were analysed. All patients (mean age: 60 years, range: 19-95) were diabetics (type I or II) and had elevated levels of cholesterol and/or triglycerides. They were treated with 500 mg etofyllin clofibrate daily for 3-4 months. Baseline values expressed as means (+/-SD) have been measured as mg%: Total cholesterol: 287.6 (+/-64.6), LDL-cholesterol: 181.4 (+/-55.2), HDL-cholesterol: 37.6 (+/-12.1), triglycerides: 398.8 (+/-296.6), blood-glucose (empty stomach): 159.6 (+/-51.0), blood-glucose (2 h after meal): 191.7 (+/-52.4) and HbA1C: 8.8 (+/-2.1). Compared to baseline, the following relative changes (%) occurred after 3-4 months: Total cholesterol: -16.6 (+/-13.9), LDL-cholesterol: -17.9 (+/-25.6), HDL-cholesterol: +30.4 (+/-36.1), triglycerides: -33.3 (+/-20.8), blood-glucose (empty stomach): -8.7 (+/-19.4), blood-glucose (2 h after meal): -9.0 (+/-17.1) and HbA1C: -5.8 (+/-12.2). The "Atherogenic Index" (rate of total cholesterol to HDL-cholesterol) fell by 32.0% (+/-21.1) from 8.3 (+/-3.3) to 5.4 (+/-1.8). 42 patients reported (3.5%) side effects, which were already well known from previous clinical trials in terms of quality and quantity. It can be concluded, that etofyllin clofibrate is safe and effective in treatment by improving prognostically unfavourable lipid parameters and concomitantly reducing blood-glucose in clinically relevant amounts in high-risk patients with hyperlipidemia and diabetes. Thus, many risk-factors for coronary heart disease associated with an increase in morbidity and mortality were markedly improved.
